<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/rudra-pratap-singh"><span class="enc-name">Rudra Pratap Singh</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rudra Pratap Singh was a Bundela Rajput chief who founded Orchha in Bundelkhand in 1531, on an island in the Betwa river, and made it his capital.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rudra-singha"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rudra-singha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rudra Singha</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rudra Singha, or Sukhrungphaa, was king of the Ahom kingdom of Assam from 1696 to 1714, under whom the state reached the height of its power.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/rudrabhatta"><span class="enc-name">Rudrabhatta</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rudrabhatta was a Kannada poet of the Hoysala period, patronised by a minister of the king Veera Ballala II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rudradaman-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rudradaman-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rudradaman I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rudradaman I was a ruler of the Western Satraps in the mid-2nd century CE and a grandson of Chastana.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/rudradeva-kakatiya"><span class="enc-name">Rudradeva (Kakatiya dynasty)</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rudradeva, also called Prataparudra I, was the Kakatiya ruler who made the dynasty independent of the Western Chalukya Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/rudrasena-i"><span class="enc-name">Rudrasena I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rudrasena I was a king of the Vakataka dynasty in cen