="enc-snip">The Rwandan Revolution, or Hutu Revolution, was a period of violence and political change in Rwanda from 1959 to 1961 that ended the Tutsi-led monarchy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rwenzori-mountains"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rwenzori-mountains.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rwenzori Mountains</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Rwenzori Mountains are a range on the border between Uganda and the Democratic Republic of the Congo, rising to 5,109 metres at Margherita Peak on Mount Stanley.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ryangombe"><span class="enc-name">Ryangombe</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Ryangombe is a legendary hero and spirit at the centre of the kubandwa cult of Rwanda and neighbouring lands, known in Burundi as Kiranga.</span></a></li></ul>
